-- title:
--   Finite generation of the level-Γ_H(q²M') q-expansion field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` for the residue field of $A$, and let $H =$ `levelH q M'` be the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$ induced by $q \mid q^2 M'$. Consider the field $E =$ `xHFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,(q^2M')\,H$, namely the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the set `intFormRatiosC` $\kappa\,\Gamma$ of ratios of integral forms for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $(q^2M')\,H$, the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the determinant-type character `gamma0Units` on $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$. The assertion is that there exists an element $t \in E$ such that $E$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\kappa(t)$ generated by $t$ over $\kappa$.
--
--   This is the statement that the reduced ($q$-expansion) function field of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ over the residue field $\kappa$ is a finite extension of a rational subfield $\kappa(t)$, i.e. is finitely generated of transcendence degree one in the strong form needed to treat it as the function field of a curve over $\kappa$. It is the $q = 3$ case of this finiteness input, and is used further on in the semistable-reduction analysis of the Igusa tower, for instance in the identification of places and of integral models over $\kappa$ in characteristic $q$.
